    "areas": [
     [
      -0.08,
      51.51,
      0.25,
      "rgba(200,48,42,.35)"
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And the security system was, well, one old man."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Talbot Edwards, keeper of the jewels, was seventy-seven years old and lived upstairs with his family.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "castle",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "edwards",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "happy",
      "pose": "wave"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "edwards",
     "text": "Talbot Edwards, keeper of the jewels"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "For a fee, he'd show the jewels to visitors. Yes. You could just ask."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Enter Thomas Blood, an Irish-born adventurer who'd already been caught up in plots against the government.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "street",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.45,
      "mood": "smug",
      "pose": "hips",
      "enter": "right"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "pan"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "In the spring of 1671 he showed up dressed as a parson, with a woman posing as his wife."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "She suddenly felt ill, the Edwards family helped her, and a friendship was born."
  },
  {
   "who": "edwards",
   "say": "Such a kind parson! Do come again.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "edwards",
      "x": 0.3,
      "mood": "happy"
     },
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "smug",
      "pose": "present"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "blood",
   "say": "Oh, I will. And next time, I'll bring my nephew. He's single."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Over the next weeks Blood kept visiting, and offered to match his nephew with the Edwards's daughter.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "smug",
      "pose": "think"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "blood"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "On the big day, the ninth of May, Blood arrived with his son playing the nephew, plus three other men."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Once the jewel room was unlocked, the gang attacked the old keeper and went for the treasure.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "vault",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.35,
      "mood": "shout"
     },
     {
      "id": "robber1",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "smug",
      "hold": "goldbar"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "shake",
    "fx": [
     "dust"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Blood flattened the crown with the mallet, one man shoved the orb down his trousers, and another tried to saw the sceptre in half."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Then, in perfect sitcom timing, Edwards's son came home from abroad, and the alarm went up.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "street",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "run",
      "mood": "scared",
      "walk": [
       0.2,
       0.7
      ]
     }
    ],
    "fx": [
     "dust"
    ],
    "cam": "pan"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Blood was caught before he got out of the Tower area, reportedly still hanging on to the crown."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And according to the story, he wasn't even embarrassed.",
   "show": {
    "k": "quote",
    "text": "It was a gallant attempt, however unsuccessful! It was for a crown!",
    "who": "Colonel Thomas Blood on his arrest, as traditionally reported (1671)"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Blood refused to explain himself to anyone but the king. And somehow, King Charles the Second agreed to see him.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "throne",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "charles",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "neutral"
     },
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "smug",
      "pose": "hips"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "charles",
   "say": "So. You're the man who tried to steal my crown.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "throne",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "charles",
      "x": 0.3,
      "pose": "sit",
      "mood": "angry"
     },
     {
      "id": "blood",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "happy",
      "pose": "present"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "charles"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "blood",
   "say": "Your Majesty, I'd call it borrowing, with enthusiasm."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Nobody knows exactly what was said. But Blood walked out pardoned, with Irish land said to be worth five hundred pounds a year."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Historians still argue about why. Maybe charm, maybe he was useful as a spy. Either way, the jewels got proper armed guards after that.",
   "show": {
    "k": "card",
    "label": "Blood's reward, instead of punishment",
    "big": "£500 A YEAR",
    "sub": "in Irish land, as usually reported, plus a royal pardon",
