    "areas": [
     [
      -6.27,
      53.34,
      0.3,
      "rgba(31,138,74,.35)"
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Ireland's so-called Crown Jewels weren't a crown at all. They were the jewelled star and badge of the Order of Saint Patrick."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Think diamonds, rubies and emeralds, worn by the order's top knight on very fancy occasions."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "They sat in a safe in Dublin Castle, in the care of Sir Arthur Vicars, the Ulster King of Arms.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "castle",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vicars",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "smug",
      "pose": "hips"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "vicars",
     "text": "Sir Arthur Vicars"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Great title. Less great with keys."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "On the sixth of July, 1907, the safe was opened, and the jewels were simply gone.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "office",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vicars",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "shock",
      "pose": "scared"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "GONE",
      "at": 1.3,
      "color": "#C8302A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "vicars",
   "say": "They were right here! I'm almost sure they were right here!"
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The lock hadn't been forced. Whoever took them either had a key or knew where to find one."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And the timing was terrible. Four days later, King Edward the Seventh arrived for a visit.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "edward7",
      "x": 0.35,
      "mood": "angry",
      "pose": "hips"
     },
     {
      "id": "vicars",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "scared"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "edward7",
     "text": "King Edward VII"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "edward7",
   "say": "So. Where exactly are my Irish jewels?"
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The ceremony that needed them was cancelled, Vicars lost his job, and rumours flew in every direction."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "One suspect was a member of his own staff, Francis Shackleton, brother of the polar explorer Ernest Shackleton. He was never charged."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Nobody was ever charged. More than a century later, the jewels have never been found.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "castle",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "vicars",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "sad",
      "pose": "shrug"
     }
    ],
    "fx": [
     "rain"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "So if you ever find a diamond star in your great-grandma's attic, maybe make a phone call."
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
