  {
   "who": "beroud",
   "say": "Excuse me. Where is the Mona Lisa?"
  },
  {
   "who": "lguard",
   "say": "Being photographed, probably. Relax.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "beroud",
      "x": 0.3,
      "mood": "angry",
      "pose": "hips"
     },
     {
      "id": "lguard",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "smug",
      "pose": "shrug"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "lguard"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "She was not being photographed. The Louvre shut for a week while police searched."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Police even questioned the poet Guillaume Apollinaire and a young painter named Pablo Picasso. Neither had done it.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "courtroom",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "beroud",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "scared"
     }
    ],
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "WRONG GUYS",
      "at": 1.4,
      "color": "#C8302A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Meanwhile, crowds lined up to stare at the empty spot on the wall. The painting got more famous by being gone."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And where was she? In Peruggia's room in Paris, hidden in a trunk, for more than two years.",
   "show": {
    "k": "card",
    "label": "Time the Mona Lisa was missing",
    "big": "2+ YEARS",
    "sub": "August 1911 to December 1913",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "peruggia",
      "x": 0.85,
      "mood": "smug"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "In December 1913, Peruggia took her to Florence and offered her to an art dealer named Alfredo Geri.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": 6.5,
    "lat": 46.5,
    "z0": 1.8,
    "z1": 2.2,
    "labels": [
     [
      "Paris",
      2.35,
      48.86,
      14
     ],
     [
      "Florence",
      11.25,
      43.77,
      14
     ]
    ],
    "route": [
     [
      2.35,
      48.86
     ],
     [
      6.0,
      46.2
     ],
     [
      8.9,
      44.4
     ],
     [
      11.25,
      43.77
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "geri",
   "say": "Magnificent! Let me just show it to a friend.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "office",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "peruggia",
      "x": 0.3,
      "mood": "happy",
      "pose": "present"
     },
     {
      "id": "geri",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "smug"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "geri",
     "text": "Alfredo Geri"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "The friend was the director of the Uffizi Gallery. The police arrived soon after."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Peruggia said he did it to return her to Italy. He got a short prison sentence, and the Mona Lisa went home to Paris more famous than ever.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "palace",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "peruggia",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "sad",
      "pose": "shrug"
     }
    ],
    "fx": [
     "confetti"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "chapter",
    "year": "1934",
    "title": "The Missing Judges",
    "bg": "church"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Belgium, 1934. In Saint Bavo's Cathedral in Ghent hangs the Ghent Altarpiece, painted by the van Eyck brothers in the 1400s.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": 4.0,
    "lat": 51.0,
    "z0": 3,
    "z1": 4,
    "labels": [
     [
      "Ghent",
      3.72,
      51.05,
      14
     ],
     [
      "Brussels",
      4.35,
      50.85,
      14
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "It's been stolen, sold and fought over so often that it's often called the most stolen artwork in history."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "On the night of the tenth of April, 1934, one panel vanished: The Just Judges.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "church",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "lawyer",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "shock",
      "pose": "scared"
     }
    ],
    "stickers": [
     {
      "text": "MISSING",
      "at": 1.3,
      "color": "#C8302A"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Soon, ransom letters arrived, demanding a huge sum for its return."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "To prove he was serious, the thief even gave back the painting on the panel's reverse side. Generous. Sort of."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Then, in November 1934, a stockbroker named Arsène Goedertier collapsed and called for his lawyer.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "office",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "goedertier",
      "x": 0.35,
      "mood": "sad",
      "pose": "sit"
     },
     {
      "id": "lawyer",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "neutral"
     }
    ],
    "tag": {
     "id": "goedertier",
     "text": "Arsène Goedertier"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "goedertier",
   "say": "Only I know where the Just Judges are."
  },
  {
   "who": "lawyer",
   "say": "Wonderful! And where is that?",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "office",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "goedertier",
      "x": 0.35,
      "mood": "sad",
      "pose": "sit"
     },
     {
      "id": "lawyer",
      "x": 0.7,
      "mood": "happy",
      "pose": "point"
     }
    ],
    "cam": "close",
    "focus": "lawyer"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "And then he died without telling anyone."
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "His papers held copies of the ransom letters, but no location. The panel has never been found.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "library",
    "cast": [
     {
      "id": "lawyer",
      "x": 0.5,
      "mood": "sad",
      "pose": "facepalm"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Today, a copy finished in the 1940s fills the gap, and people are still searching for the original."
  },
  {
   "hold": 2.5,
   "show": {
    "k": "chapter",
    "year": "1963",
    "title": "The Great Train Robbery",
    "bg": "field"
   }
  },
  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "England, the eighth of August, 1963, three in the morning. A Royal Mail train is heading from Glasgow to London.",
   "show": {
    "k": "map",
    "lon": -1.2,
    "lat": 52.8,
    "z0": 1.8,
    "z1": 2.4,
    "labels": [
